  "abilities": [],
  "behavior": "It behaves almost exactly like a normal scorpling: simple close-range attacks and a reliance on numbers to become a real threat.",
  "interactionWithPlayer": "On its own it remains fairly harmless, although its increased durability makes it take slightly longer to kill. The problem begins when several gather around the player while other O.R.C. creatures apply pressure.",
  "interactionWithCreatures": "It often appears in waves alongside other O.R.C. enemies, where it can surround or distract the player while more dangerous creatures attack from other angles.",
  "strategy": "Prioritize weapons or attacks with area damage to kill several at once. It is rarely worth focusing too much damage on a single one. If you are using a turret during the event, it can also clear groups of scorplings very easily because of the special O.R.C. turret vulnerability.",
